{title: More Love to Thee}
{artist: Elizabeth Prentiss & William Doane}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 72}

Verse 1
[Eb]More love to [Bb]thee, O [Eb]Christ, more [Ab]love to [Bb]thee!
[Eb]Hear thou the [Bb]prayer I [Cm]make on [Ab]bended [Bb]knee;
[Eb]this is my [Bb]earnest [Eb]plea: more [Ab]love, O [Eb]Christ, to [Bb]thee —
[Eb]more love to [Ab]thee, [Eb]more [Bb]love to [Eb]thee!

Verse 2
Once earthly joy I craved,
Sought peace and rest;
Now thee alone I seek,
Give what is best;
This all my pray'r shall be,
More love, O Christ, to Thee,
More love to Thee;
More love to Thee.

Verse 3
Then shall my latest breath,
Whisper Thy praise,
This be the parting cry
My heart shall raise;
This still its pray'r shall be,
More love, O Christ, to Thee,
More love to Thee;
More love to Thee.
